ng says what to do when a deadline has already passed.\n- No band covers 0 days late or more than 60 days late.\n- It's unclear whether \"ask once whether you can help first\" also applies during the security questions. The policy currently applies it to every request for a human.\n- No wording is given for the \"could not record it\" sentence.\n\nFiles are in `out/`:\n- lb-06.policy.json\n- lb-06.audit.json"}
{"event": "policy_compiled", "run_id": "f95c235588c8450282e710182a18cefe", "pid": 104590, "time": "2026-10-10T20:16:24-0700", "elapsed_s": 154.684, "artifact": "out/lb-06.policy.json", "bands": 3, "identity_fields": ["phone_last4", "date_of_birth", "postcode", "birth_year"], "special_cases": ["already_paid", "dispute", "hardship", "restructuring", "human", "scam", "robot", "refuse_to_talk", "change_promise"], "unresolved": [{"topic": "identity.hint_reply", "text": "The API's verify_identity returns hint `day_month_swapped`, but the documents dictate no reply for it; hint_reply left empty.", "doc": "sources/000-thread.txt"}, {"topic": "phrases.cannot_answer_sentence", "text": "The documents give no sentence for questions the agent cannot answer.", "doc": "sources/000-thread.txt"}, {"topic": "dates.past_deadline", "text": "The documents do not say what to do when the computed deadline is already in the past; default kept.", "doc": "sources/000-thread.txt"}, {"topic": "bands", "text": "The documents define bands only for 1 to 60 days late; products outside that range are not covered.", "doc": "sources/000-thread.txt"}, {"topic": "special_cases.human", "text": "Operations (7 October) says human requests: ask once whether you can help first; it does not say whether this also applies during the identity check (rule 15). It is applied to all human requests.", "doc": "sources/000-thread.txt"}, {"topic": "promise_write.failure_sentence", "text": "Rule 32 says to say you could not record the promise, but gives no wording and the schema has no phrase field for it.", "doc": "sources/000-thread.txt"}], "audit_fixed": ["special_cases[human].source: the quote was mislabelled. It presented the 1 Oct rule 29 text ('do not ask whether you can help') as the overriding Operations text. Replaced it with Operations 7 Oct point 4 ('ask once whether you can help first'), noting that this overrides rule 29. The values were already correct.", "identity.source, outcomes.source, phrases.source, promise_write.source: added the quotes that support holder_confirmation_asks, goodbye_before_close, today_question and confirm_phrase/one_promise_per_product.", "unresolved: added an entry for the rule 32 'say you could not record it' sentence, which has no dictated wording and no phrase field."], "audit_unresolved": ["No reply is dictated for the verify_identity hint `day_month_swapped`, so hint_reply is empty.", "No sentence is given for questions the agent cannot answer.", "The documents do not say what happens when a computed deadline is already in the past.", "No band covers products more than 60 days late or 0 days late.", "It is unclear whether 'ask once whether you can help first' (7 Oct) also applies to human requests during the identity check (rule 15). It is applied to all human requests.", "No wording is given for the 'could not record it' sentence after a failed create_promise."], "defaulted_without_source": []}
